{
  "abstract": "For every n, 2^(n(n+3)) divides the (n+1)×(n+1) Hankel determinant det[a(i+j)] of the Catalan–Larcombe–French numbers a, and the quotient is a positive odd integer. This is Zhi-Wei Sun's conjecture (2013), proved by Zhu and Sun (2018).",
